p.src:
Nicole gives the lecture’s sharpest libertarian rebuttal. She does not deny that teachers, builders, and institutions mattered. She denies the inference from help to continuing debt. Roads were built by people who were paid. Teachers were not teaching for free. The relevant debts, on this view, have already been discharged through salary, price, or public compensation: $\text{price system payment for roads, teachers, labor}
\Longrightarrow
\text{no continuing debt to society}.$

