p.src:
She then concedes luck but still blocks the redistributionist conclusion. Michael Jordan may be lucky to be gifted, but luck alone does not generate a claim on his earnings: $\text{luck alone}
\not\Longrightarrow
\text{society has a claim on earnings}.$ And if we do allow such a claim, Nicole argues, we begin to claim not only part of the fruits of labor but, in a weaker and more troubling sense, part of the laboring person as well.

