p.src:
At the very end, once the corrupted transcript clears again, Sandel returns to Obama’s original phrase: You didn’t build it. What Obama seemed to invoke, Sandel says, was indebtedness, and perhaps luck as well. If you are successful, you should recognize the invisible help behind your success and not inhale too deeply of your own achievement. Sandel grants that this argument has moral force. But he then asks the question toward which the whole lecture has been moving: $\text{luck} + \text{indebtedness}
\stackrel{?}{\Longrightarrow}
\text{adequate argument for the welfare state}.$

